{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Let them lift up.</b> [Their] voice:" "<b>The desert and its cities, etc.</b> And all the settlements where Kedar dwells — and behold, the Kedarites are always in the desert:" "<b>Let them cry out.</b> The nations, inhabitants of Sela, let them lift up [their] voice, like \"and the cry passed\" (1 Kings 22:26):" "<b>Let them shout.</b> Raising the voice for praise or for blame, and like it \"a cry over the wine\" (Isaiah 24:11):"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:33.911043728Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}